    "result": "Perfect! My implementation is complete and the tests are passing. Let me create a summary of what I've implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully implemented the `--threshold` feature for `frai eval` as requested. Here's what was added:\n\n### Core Changes (frai-core)\n\n1. **Enhanced `generateReport` function** (`packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.js`):\n   - Added optional `thresholds` parameter accepting an object like `{ exact_match: 0.9 }`\n   - Calculates which thresholds pass/fail based on metric scores\n   - Returns `passed` (boolean) and `thresholds` (array with `{ metric, min, score, passed }` entries)\n   - Handles null scores as failed thresholds\n\n2. **Updated markdown reporter** (`packages/frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js`):\n   - Added \"Thresholds\" section showing PASS/FAIL status for each threshold\n\n3. **Added comprehensive tests** (`packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.test.js`):\n   - Tests for passing thresholds\n   - Tests for failing thresholds  \n   - Tests for null scores as failures\n\n### CLI Changes (frai-cli)\n\n1. **Added threshold parsing** (`packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`):\n   - New `parseThresholds()` function validates:\n     - Format: `<metric>=<number>` (e.g., `exact_match=0.9`)\n     - Values between 0 and 1\n     - Known metric IDs (exact_match, toxicity, length_variance)\n   - Exits with code 2 on malformed input\n\n2. **Updated `runEvalCommand`**:\n   - Passes thresholds to `generateReport`\n   - Exits with code 1 if any threshold fails, 0 if all pass\n   - Report is written either way\n\n3. **Added `--threshold` option** to eval command:\n   - Can be used multiple times: `--threshold exact_match=0.9 --threshold toxicity=0.95`\n   - Documented in CLI help\n\n### Documentation\n\nUpdated both READMEs with:\n- CLI option documentation for `--threshold`\n- SDK example showing how to use thresholds programmatically\n- Clear explanation of exit codes and behavior\n\n**Test Status**: 5 new threshold tests passing